From 6e291167c956bce71dfd3a2671b61218385edc9d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: useraccessdenied <useraccessdenied@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 10:14:02 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 15/29] pinctrl: pinconf-generic: check bitmap_zalloc() in
 parse_fw_cfg()

parse_fw_cfg() passes the result of bitmap_zalloc() to test_and_set_bit()
without checking it. Found with a deterministic fail-nth sweep over a
driver probe on a KASAN kernel: failing that allocation oopses in
pinconf_generic_parse_dt_config() via pinctrl_bind_pins() during probe.
Return -ENOMEM instead.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/pinctrl/pinconf-generic.c | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/pinctrl/pinconf-generic.c b/drivers/pinctrl/pinconf-generic.c
index 95c803c40..5205809e5 100644
--- a/drivers/pinctrl/pinconf-generic.c
+++ b/drivers/pinctrl/pinconf-generic.c
@@ -229,6 +229,9 @@ static int parse_fw_cfg(struct fwnode_handle *fwnode,
 
 	unsigned long *properties __free(bitmap) = bitmap_zalloc(count, GFP_KERNEL);
 
+	if (!properties)
+		return -ENOMEM;
+
 	for (i = 0; i < count; i++) {
 		u32 val;
 		int ret;
